\section{Final comments}

After the submission of this manuscript, the authors obtained a few straightforward improvements of~\Cref{thm:d squared intro}. First,  the simulation can be made round preserving, where the classical algorithm is itself also a $d$-round parallel algorithm. Second, a tighter analysis results in an improved classical query complexity of $t^{O(d)}$. These proofs will appear in an accompanying  note~\cite{BDST26}. 

